    "body": "STOPPED: The quick gate failed twice on the same source tree. The claim is released.\n\nBoth runs failed post_not_judged::not_judged_with_no_generator_verdict_blocks. The test expects one problem. It receives two problems for Face1.\n\nThe new posting_waterjet::problems clause returns a generic program_ops error. The stock simulation clause already reports this error. The fixture has no waterjet operation.\n\nThe next attempt should keep generic program errors out of the waterjet clause. It should pin this case before it changes the clause.\n\nThe nine waterjet regression pins failed with the old source and passed with the fix. The suppression control passed. All four source restoration checks passed their red and green runs.\n\nThe quick runs each completed 331 checks with one failure. The UI suite passed 1532 tests and ignored eight tests. The example catalog passed 39 tests and ignored four tests. The waterjet CL golden passed. No NC or CL golden changed.\n\nThe heavy gate and strict clippy did not run. Step 7 requires this stop after two real failures.\n\nThe patch remains local in .claude/worktrees/issue-3637 on issue/3637-waterjet-safety. No commit, push, or PR exists for this attempt. The worktree also contains the gate logs. The screenshots remain in /tmp. No process file changed.\n",
